id: pm-sxg7wl
title: "GH-1148: cached drift mismatch can falsely report tracker corruption"
description: "GitHub issue #1148 demonstrates that pm health can combine stat-trusted history and item metadata caches into a history_drift_hash_mismatch verdict that strict authoritative rereads disprove, while the diagnostic omits cache invalidation evidence and remediation."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:health","area:history","area:sdk",cache-integrity,context-integrity,github-1148
created_at: "2026-08-29T00:20:31.873Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-29T03:06:34.907Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-29T03:06:06.037Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-29T03:06:06.037Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Metadata-mode health preserves the warm-cache fast path when cached hashes agree; A cached hash mismatch is never emitted until the item document and history stream are reread authoritatively; Stale cache evidence is replaced and the final diagnostic reports that a strict confirmation occurred; Cache schema records the runtime history-hash capability and invalidates incompatible envelopes; Regression and performance controls cover false-positive recovery, genuine drift retention, and zero extra rereads on clean cache hits; SDK CLI health validate and temporary-workspace acceptance retain contract parity and exact coverage"
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: high
confidence: high
reporter: GitHub issue #1148
severity: high
environment: pm 2026.8.24 and 2026.8.28 on a clean long-lived pm-brief workspace
repro_steps: "Prime history and metadata caches, restore an older stat-compatible cache state through ordinary git/package operations, then run pm health and compare the hash-mismatch verdict with an authoritative cache-free scan."
resolution: "Fixed: authoritative drift confirmation now reloads current history streams, replaces stale cache evidence, and emits the correct resolved false-positive summary field."
expected_result: "Metadata cache hits remain fast, but every suspected corruption or writer-version skew is confirmed from fresh item and history evidence before health reports it."
actual_result: "Fresh-stream regression, linked health acceptance, full exact coverage, static assurance, defect evidence, record integrity, and secret scanning pass."
component: "SDK health, history drift cache, metadata cache, and diagnostics"
customer_impact: A false corruption warning can block releases or induce an agent to rewrite correct immutable history.
