comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-29T00:20:31.873Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence: complete 2596-item all-status strict read had no omissions; corpus-wide cache search found 20 historical or strategic candidates. Closed pm-up22 owns stat-preserving false-clean prevention, closed pm-c90s owns the intentional metadata health fast path, and closed pm-2qahia owns writer-version skew. None owns the new false-corruption confirmation failure reported by GitHub #1148, so this recurrence is canonical."
  "2026-08-29T00:27:16.900Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: SDK health keeps metadata verification for clean cache hits, but any cached hash, chain, or writer-version candidate now forces canonical item enumeration plus strict stream content hashing. Diagnostics publish candidate, confirmed, and resolved-false-positive sets. History drift cache schema v5 binds the current item-hash capability so incompatible cache meaning is never reused. Focused 73-test regression suite, ESLint, TypeScript projects, and diff hygiene pass."
  "2026-08-29T00:40:45.398Z","harness:codex","Final verification evidence: full repository coverage passed 586 files and 8,101 tests at exactly 60,128/60,128 statements, 45,317/45,317 branches, 12,500/12,500 functions, and 57,900/57,900 lines. Repository static assurance, SDK/package parity, contract snapshots, agent context/token gates, graph and record-integrity assurances, ESLint, both jscpd profiles with zero clones, TypeScript projects, secret scan, and git diff hygiene all pass. The existing packed npm/Bun/Node SDK and CLI temporary-workspace acceptance remains green for this delivery."
  "2026-08-29T02:22:17.210Z","harness:codex","Review-round evidence: brief health cache-confirmation vectors are bounded, unsupported cached hash capability rows invalidate regardless of legacy version_skew shape, and confirmed chain corruption remains independent from version skew. The 74-test linked health/drift suite, static gates, and exact coverage pass."
  "2026-08-29T03:05:20.911Z","harness:codex","Second review-round evidence: strict and content drift verification now always reload authoritative stream evidence before confirming or clearing a cache candidate, so a forged cached writer-version result cannot survive an unchanged content hash. The brief health summary now emits the actual resolved_false_positive_items field. Focused drift/health regressions and the complete 8,108-test exact-coverage gate pass."
  "2026-08-29T03:06:04.100Z","harness:codex","Linked acceptance: pm test-all selected all four active items and passed 4/4 with 2 executed commands, 2 intentional duplicate skips, zero failures; drift/health executed 75 tests."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-29T00:40:44.988Z","harness:codex","Cache evidence can safely accelerate a clean verdict, but a corruption verdict is a higher-trust claim: promote it through canonical source reads and content hashing before exposing it to agents. Bind persisted cache semantics to the hash-writer capability so version drift invalidates evidence rather than reinterpreting it."
